---
title: "generate_referral_code (protocol::referral)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_sender: self, random, ctx
    q_get_sender --> q_check_existing: sender = ctx.sender()
    q_check_existing --> q_error_exists: self.referrer_code.contains(sender)
    q_check_existing --> q_check_qualified: !self.referrer_code.contains(sender)
    q_error_exists --> [*]: abort referral_already_has_referral_code()
    q_check_qualified --> q_error_not_qualified: !self.is_qualified_to_create_referral_code(sender)
    q_check_qualified --> q_generate: self.is_qualified_to_create_referral_code(sender)
    q_error_not_qualified --> [*]: abort referral_not_qualified_to_gen_code()
    q_generate --> q_check_unique: referral_code = generate_random_string(random, 6, ctx)
    q_check_unique --> q_error_collision: self.code_owner.contains(referral_code)
    q_check_unique --> q_store: !self.code_owner.contains(referral_code)
    q_error_collision --> [*]: abort referral_invalid_referral_code()
    q_store --> q_store2: self.code_owner.add(referral_code, sender)
    q_store2 --> [*]: self.referrer_code.add(sender, referral_code)

    note right of q_generate
        INV-001: Each address can have at most one referral code
        INV-002: Sender must meet deposit threshold to generate code
        INV-003: Generated code is 6 chars from a-z, 0-9
        INV-004: code_owner and referrer_code maintain bidirectional mapping
        INV-005: Aborts on collision rather than retrying (single attempt)
    end note
